        "After the customer walkthrough, what do the salespeople do?",
        "What can experiencing a customer's process reveal?"
      ],
      "notes": "- Timer: 3 minutes. Students answer alone, from memory; then compare with a partner.\n- Practice only. The knowledge-test bank is a draft and is not approved for graded use.\nAnswers:\n- 1. Pictures unrelated to the problem area (Michalko 2010, 440).\n- 2. Discuss it, develop new ideas or modifications, and record them (Michalko 2010, 440).\n- 3. Behaviors, words, and actions that affect the customer's attitude (Michalko 2010, 371).\n- 4. Share their experiences and discuss ways to improve their own service (Michalko 2010, 371).\n- 5. What talking about another person's position alone cannot (Michalko 2010, 371).\nAsk: Which answer needs another look before Lab?",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Give each group member a folder containing two or three pictures that are not related to the problem area.",
          "cite": "Michalko 2010, 440"
        },
